{"vulnerabilidade_identificada":"Persisted Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) in the 'comment' field of Feedback model.","causa_da_vulnerabilidade":"The sanitization function 'security.sanitizeHtml' used when the persistedXssFeedbackChallenge is enabled does not properly sanitize the input, allowing malicious HTML such as <iframe src="javascript:alert(`xss`)"> to be stored and later rendered, leading to XSS.","estrategia_de_correcao":"Replace the insecure sanitization function 'security.sanitizeHtml' with the more secure 'security.sanitizeSecure' for all cases, ensuring that all comments are properly sanitized to prevent XSS regardless of challenge state.","edicoes":[{"arquivo":"models/feedback.ts","trecho_original":"          if (utils.isChallengeEnabled(challenges.persistedXssFeedbackChallenge)) {
            sanitizedComment = security.sanitizeHtml(comment)
            challengeUtils.solveIf(challenges.persistedXssFeedbackChallenge, () => {
              return utils.contains(
                sanitizedComment,
                '<iframe src="javascript:alert(`xss`)">'
              )
            })
          } else {
            sanitizedComment = security.sanitizeSecure(comment)
          }","trecho_corrigido":"          sanitizedComment = security.sanitizeSecure(comment)
          if (utils.isChallengeEnabled(challenges.persistedXssFeedbackChallenge)) {
            challengeUtils.solveIf(challenges.persistedXssFeedbackChallenge, () => {
              return utils.contains(
                sanitizedComment,
                '<iframe src="javascript:alert(`xss`)">'
              )
            })
          }"}],"justificativa_tecnica":"The original code uses 'security.sanitizeHtml' when the persistedXssFeedbackChallenge is enabled, which is insufficient to prevent XSS attacks because it allows dangerous HTML tags like <iframe> with javascript: URLs. By always using 'security.sanitizeSecure', which presumably applies a stricter sanitization, we ensure that all user input is properly sanitized before storage, mitigating the risk of persisted XSS. The challenge detection logic is preserved and moved after sanitization to maintain existing functionality.","limitacoes_da_correcao":"This fix assumes that 'security.sanitizeSecure' provides adequate sanitization against XSS. If the sanitization function is not comprehensive, additional measures might be necessary. Also, this change disables the intentional vulnerability for the persistedXssFeedbackChallenge, which might affect challenge completion if the challenge relies on the vulnerability."}
